{:edb/db-before-t 2619 :edb/db-after-t 2620 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535932 50 #inst "2026-10-09T10:55:28.315Z" 13194139535932 true] [17592186129146 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375153 13194139535932 true] [17592186129219 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375139 13194139535932 true] [17592186129219 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375146 13194139535932 true] [17592186129220 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375160 13194139535932 true] [17592186129220 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375167 13194139535932 true] [17592186375139 1017 #edb/ref 17592186375140 13194139535932 true] [17592186375139 1089 "q-163178" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375139 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535932 true] [17592186375139 1100 "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}.$\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to its distance from the $y$-axis.\nFind the moment of inertia of the lamina about the origin." 13194139535932 true] [17592186375139 1113 #uuid "1e6284a1-bc66-56ea-88f9-e7e54514c1d3" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375139 1145 "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFrom the description, the mass density function can be written as\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=k|x|=kx,\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find an expression for $k$ in terms of $M$ by integrating the density function over the plate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}kx\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =k({\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =k{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{1}\\cdot [y]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =k(\\frac{1}{2}-0)(2-0) \\\\  & =k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=M$ and hence $\\lambda (x,y)=kx=Mx.$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =M{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =M{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =M{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =M{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =M{[\\frac{1}{4}y+\\frac{1}{6}{y}^{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =M(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{4}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{11M}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375140 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375141 13194139535932 true] [17592186375140 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375142 13194139535932 true] [17592186375140 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375143 13194139535932 true] [17592186375140 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375144 13194139535932 true] [17592186375140 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375145 13194139535932 true] [17592186375140 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535932 true] [17592186375140 1041 "selection" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375140 1104 #edb/ref 17592186375144 13194139535932 true] [17592186375140 1110 #uuid "5765c3ab-4009-54e6-8878-aa6b6d014a43" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375141 1034 "\\frac{13M}{3}" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375141 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535932 true] [17592186375141 1111 #uuid "0b616b3f-8c29-5668-a92f-d2152097de09" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375142 1034 "\\frac{6M}{5}" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375142 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535932 true] [17592186375142 1111 #uuid "d2fbbaa7-5124-52eb-94c1-eddee930bd3c" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375143 1034 "\\frac{7M}{4}" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375143 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535932 true] [17592186375143 1111 #uuid "adac2438-fe96-5915-a0c5-c4025c1dabfa" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375144 1034 "\\frac{11M}{6}" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375144 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535932 true] [17592186375144 1111 #uuid "c86b11f8-95d7-5535-9b3d-6aeb5a2c8cea" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375145 1034 "\\frac{9M}{2}" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375145 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535932 true] [17592186375145 1111 #uuid "4e6cf357-2c39-5e11-8f5e-86a70316071b" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375146 1017 #edb/ref 17592186375147 13194139535932 true] [17592186375146 1089 "q-163199" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375146 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535932 true] [17592186375146 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072087/assets/a39a8998e4e1ae9f6ed8095b124ba31db5f3b4ffb699db815ef03144479f798c.png)\n\nA triangular plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ in the first quadrant enclosed by the line $y=2-2x$ and the coordinate axes. The mass density at each point is proportional to its distance from the $x$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the $x$-axis." 13194139535932 true] [17592186375146 1113 #uuid "e83c134b-44f9-501f-a3c1-44e8c69c1923" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375146 1145 "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2-2x},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072087/assets/aad890b85e9984fdab58a2fa15e00fad4b384a086346ad77f49f68a746e73b3a.png)\n\nFrom the description, the mass density function can be written as\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=k|y|=ky,\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find an expression for $k$ in terms of $M$ by integrating the density function over the plate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2-2x}ky\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2-2x}y\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{2-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{2}(2-2x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2k{\\int }_{0}^{1}(1-x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2k{[-\\frac{1}{3}(1-x)^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2k\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2k}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=\\frac{3M}{2}$ and hence,\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=ky=\\frac{3M}{2}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2-2x}{y}^{2}(y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2-2x}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{4}]}_{0}^{2-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{4}(2-2x)^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(1-x)^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6M{[-\\frac{1}{5}(1-x)^{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =6M\\cdot \\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{6M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375147 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375148 13194139535932 true] [17592186375147 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375149 13194139535932 true] [17592186375147 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375150 13194139535932 true] [17592186375147 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375151 13194139535932 true] [17592186375147 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375152 13194139535932 true] [17592186375147 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535932 true] [17592186375147 1041 "selection" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375147 1104 #edb/ref 17592186375148 13194139535932 true] [17592186375147 1110 #uuid "0d00460a-e0c0-5baa-932f-e073b49bcba9" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375148 1034 "\\frac{6M}{5}" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375148 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535932 true] [17592186375148 1111 #uuid "62c796d5-f4c2-5396-a2a2-671d8961d0a0" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375149 1034 "\\frac{2M}{3}" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375149 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535932 true] [17592186375149 1111 #uuid "fa8cf67a-17d5-5e7c-ae8f-6eb05b046314" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375150 1034 "3M" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375150 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535932 true] [17592186375150 1111 #uuid "d45e6a1b-6e80-5a91-a56c-dcb8dd6a30c1" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375151 1034 "2M" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375151 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535932 true] [17592186375151 1111 #uuid "e1b210e4-2aab-5b0a-9a6e-487a756d5029" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375152 1034 "\\frac{M}{6}" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375152 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535932 true] [17592186375152 1111 #uuid "488c1497-ebc1-573f-b4ff-b1f13bbd2827" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375153 1017 #edb/ref 17592186375154 13194139535932 true] [17592186375153 1089 "q-163201" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375153 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535932 true] [17592186375153 1100 "A rectangular plate of mass $M\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3},$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the $x$-axis." 13194139535932 true] [17592186375153 1113 #uuid "57ea89e8-0c9b-5d24-bdf3-e0ad277ceb7a" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375153 1145 "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 3=6.$ \n\nSince the plate has uniform density, every unit of area contains the same amount of mass. Therefore, the mass density is constant and is given by the total mass divided by the total area:\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{6}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for ${I}_{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{2}[x]_{1}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{[\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9}\\cdot 27 \\\\  & =3M.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia is $3M\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375154 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375155 13194139535932 true] [17592186375154 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375156 13194139535932 true] [17592186375154 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375157 13194139535932 true] [17592186375154 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375158 13194139535932 true] [17592186375154 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375159 13194139535932 true] [17592186375154 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535932 true] [17592186375154 1041 "selection" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375154 1104 #edb/ref 17592186375155 13194139535932 true] [17592186375154 1110 #uuid "59391a26-8846-55bd-aaa8-c9d547baa026" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375155 1034 "3M\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375155 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535932 true] [17592186375155 1111 #uuid "2b1933e7-b0f4-59f0-afd8-0ed159ecb31e" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375156 1034 "6M\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375156 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535932 true] [17592186375156 1111 #uuid "20829c67-da71-5bb4-b591-08a2c79b8a58" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375157 1034 "2M\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375157 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535932 true] [17592186375157 1111 #uuid "2196a0f3-55f1-52ca-81a0-dccbb6f3035b" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375158 1034 "\\frac{2M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375158 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535932 true] [17592186375158 1111 #uuid "29cb3e2a-9737-59c8-a406-c325175189df" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375159 1034 "\\frac{3M}{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375159 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535932 true] [17592186375159 1111 #uuid "b2c04648-7503-508e-82a1-9c719bbd393d" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375160 1017 #edb/ref 17592186375161 13194139535932 true] [17592186375160 1089 "q-163230" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375160 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535932 true] [17592186375160 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072087/assets/ad7c939aded3f5e5e1e2f3b5e5743609e331625479c25f6a55659be730ed1cf5.png)\n\nConsider the plate that occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the polar circles $r=1$ and $r=\\sqrt[5]{2}$ and the polar rays $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ in the first quadrant, as shown above. The mass density function of the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=15y.$ Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the $y$-axis." 13194139535932 true] [17592186375160 1113 #uuid "d3477445-962a-5ca7-b288-2cda1a3c304e" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375160 1145 "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (r,\\theta ),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFirst, note that the region $D$ in polar coordinates can be expressed as\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le r\\le \\sqrt[5]{2},\\,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{3}}.\n$$\n\nAlso, the mass density function in polar coordinates is \n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=15r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt[5]{2}}15r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot {r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt[5]{2}}15{r}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =({\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt[5]{2}}5{r}^{4}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & ={r}^{5}\\,{|}_{1}^{\\sqrt[5]{2}}\\cdot (-{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta )\\,{|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =(2-1)\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{8}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}-1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375161 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375162 13194139535932 true] [17592186375161 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375163 13194139535932 true] [17592186375161 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375164 13194139535932 true] [17592186375161 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375165 13194139535932 true] [17592186375161 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375166 13194139535932 true] [17592186375161 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535932 true] [17592186375161 1041 "selection" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375161 1104 #edb/ref 17592186375165 13194139535932 true] [17592186375161 1110 #uuid "2596bbad-453a-5df9-809e-34635ec7cf85" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375162 1034 "15\\sqrt{2}" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375162 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535932 true] [17592186375162 1111 #uuid "01098d48-3e4c-51b6-a8bf-3cebf03b5bc7" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375163 1034 "\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4}" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375163 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535932 true] [17592186375163 1111 #uuid "93b12471-9305-53b7-a9f2-8fb44e2e3501" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375164 1034 "4\\sqrt{2}-1" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375164 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535932 true] [17592186375164 1111 #uuid "ab5490eb-2bb5-5c3e-86ba-86fcf0f47b8c" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375165 1034 "\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}-1}{8}" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375165 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535932 true] [17592186375165 1111 #uuid "22fa9d70-a89d-5116-ba98-2455f748c2ed" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375166 1034 "8\\sqrt{2}" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375166 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535932 true] [17592186375166 1111 #uuid "51c574d7-1ec9-52e1-a22a-f81bd618dafa" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375167 1017 #edb/ref 17592186375168 13194139535932 true] [17592186375167 1089 "q-163496" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375167 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535932 true] [17592186375167 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072087/assets/3f9732e0b81ba2e171a0464996e7b0d27aa47a0b32da59fa40cbba0cdbf8402a.png)\n\nConsider a plate of mass $M$ that occupies the region $D$ bounded by the polar circles $r=1$ and $r=2,$ as shown above. The mass density at any point is proportional to its distance from the origin. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the $y$-axis." 13194139535932 true] [17592186375167 1113 #uuid "e2a29f50-8943-507c-b081-89c00f734edd" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375167 1145 "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (r,\\theta ),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D,$ in polar coordinates, can be expressed as\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le r\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nFrom the description, the mass density function can be written as $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=kr,$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find an expression for $k$ in terms of $M$ by integrating the density function over the plate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{2}kr\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{2}k{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =k({\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =k\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{r}^{3}\\,{|}_{1}^{2}\\cdot \\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =k\\cdot \\frac{7}{3}\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{14\\pi k}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=kr=\\frac{3M}{14\\pi }r.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{3M}{14\\pi }r\\cdot {r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{14\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{14\\pi }({\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{4}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{14\\pi }({\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{4}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{14\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}{r}^{5}\\,{|}_{1}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}\\theta +\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta ){|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{14\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{31}{5}\\cdot \\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{93M}{70}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375168 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375169 13194139535932 true] [17592186375168 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375170 13194139535932 true] [17592186375168 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375171 13194139535932 true] [17592186375168 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375172 13194139535932 true] [17592186375168 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375173 13194139535932 true] [17592186375168 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535932 true] [17592186375168 1041 "selection" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375168 1104 #edb/ref 17592186375173 13194139535932 true] [17592186375168 1110 #uuid "9e0c89bf-c124-5c66-9546-4320dc966592" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375169 1034 "\\frac{16M}{9}" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375169 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535932 true] [17592186375169 1111 #uuid "418734ae-9c0c-5e15-b697-a3c4709142cf" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375170 1034 "\\frac{51M}{32}" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375170 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535932 true] [17592186375170 1111 #uuid "b67f6432-6591-5208-a821-5abea4c29456" 13194139535932 true] [17592186375171 1034 "\\frac{21M}{12}" 